Good morning,

We are instructed to notify a fire loss at our client's Windrow Grove community in Tulsa. Our reference is KRP/HAB/2025/7735. The fire department's public records copy has only just been released, which is why the formal notice follows the telephone report of 21 November.

Broker reference: KRP/HAB/2025/7735
Insured name: Sundale Property Group, LLC
Claimant: Windrow Grove Apartments, LP
Date of loss: 21 November 2025
Loss location: 6120 East 91st Street, Tulsa, OK 74137 - Building K
Cause: Fire - lint ignition at a clothes dryer
Estimated loss: USD 2,610,000

Fire started in the laundry alcove of a second-floor unit at about 02:14 and got
into the attic through the dryer vent penetration. There is no draftstopping in
the attic at the unit demising lines, so it ran the length of the stack.

Two units are a total loss, all 24 in the building are uninhabitable pending
electrical clearance, and 47 residents are displaced. Two residents were treated
for smoke inhalation, one admitted overnight. No fatalities.

The dryer is landlord-provided and was installed by the client's own maintenance
department in 2019. The fire department is holding the appliance and the ducting
as evidence and will release it on a joint examination protocol - you will want
your engineer involved before anyone touches it.

Attached:

  * the completed loss notice
  * fire investigation report
  * fire loss schedule

Please confirm a claim reference and an adjuster. Tenant relocation costs are
running and our client would like your position on that head early.

